course: dictionary
lesson: 2353
title: Cub: a young animal or a young Scout
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cub is a baby animal, such as a young bear, lion, tiger, fox or wolf. Use the words around it to check its meaning. In «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears, which may help cubs follow their mother», the cubs are young tigers that follow their mother.
explain: The word has a second meaning too. A Cub, or Cub Scout, is a young member of the Scouts. Read the whole sentence first, then ask: is it talking about animals, or about children in a club?
explain: Try the swap test. In «An Arctic fox mother can have over ten cubs in a good lemming year», put «baby animals» in place of cubs and the sentence still makes sense. Put «Scouts» in and it does not, so the animal meaning fits here.
fact: A cub is a young animal, such as a bear, lion, tiger, fox or wolf.
fact: A Cub Scout is a young member of the Scouts.
fact: «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears, which may help cubs follow their mother.»
fact: «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes, which give them shade, a lookout and safe dens for cubs.»
fact: «An Arctic fox mother can have over ten cubs in a good lemming year.»
exercise: «An Arctic fox mother can have over ten cubs in a good lemming year.» What is a cub in this sentence? | A Cub Scout on a camping trip | *A young fox | A lemming | A rocky den
exercise: Mia joined the Cubs last year and learns knots and first aid. What does cub mean in this sentence? | *A young member of the Scouts | A kind of rocky hill | A bear that sleeps all winter | A baby lion
exercise: In «Serengeti lions rest on rocky outcrops called kopjes», what are kopjes? | *Rocky outcrops | Lookouts for hunters | Young lions | Safe dens for cubs
test: «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears, which may help cubs follow their mother.» Why might the spots help cubs? | *To help cubs follow their mother | To keep them warm in winter | To make them sleep | To make them look bigger
test: Ella says a cub is a young animal. Sam says a cub is a member of the Scouts. Who is right? | Only Ella, because cubs are always animals | Only Sam, because cubs are never animals | *Both are right, because cub has two meanings
exam: «Winnie the Pooh was named partly after Winnipeg, a gentle American black bear cub.» What kind of animal was Winnipeg? | A swan | *A black bear cub | A wolf cub | A lion cub
